<h2>Kericho</h2>

<p>Kenya's best-known tea region, about 260km northwest of Nairobi in the Rift
Valley highlands. Large estates, tea factories that receive visitors, and the
landscape most people picture when they think of Kenyan tea.</p>

<h2>Kiambu and Limuru</h2>

<p>The closest tea country to Nairobi, under an hour from the city. Estates
here run short factory tours and tastings, which suits a half-day visit.</p>

<h2>Nandi Hills</h2>

<p>High-altitude estates in western Kenya, producing tea with a distinct
profile from Kericho's. Fewer visitors and a longer drive.</p>

<h2>Nyeri and the Mount Kenya slopes</h2>

<p>Smallholder tea country on the southern slopes of Mount Kenya, often
combined with a visit to Aberdare or Mount Kenya national parks.</p>

<h2>Beyond tea</h2>

<p>Nairobi has a national park inside the city boundary. The Maasai Mara,
Amboseli and the coast are all reachable on domestic flights.</p>

